From: Stoicoci Mihaita <stoicocimihaita@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: cs35l45: pause the firmware before clearing GLOBAL_EN

On the Lenovo Tab P12 Pro (4x CS35L45, speaker-protection firmware
v0.37.0, DAC fed from ASP_RX) every amplifier reported "DSP Watchdog
Timer" a few seconds after the first short streams PipeWire opens at
session start, and the protection firmware stayed dead until it was
reloaded.

The firmware reports RUNNING (mailbox status 0) after it is started at
preload and runs again whenever the amplifier is enabled. When the DSP
widget is not in the DAPM path nothing sends PAUSE, so the firmware is
still running when GLOBAL_EN is cleared and the PLL loses BCLK; the
watchdog then expires 3-7 s later, also when the part was sent
HIBERNATE in between (it is not processed without a clock).

Send PAUSE before clearing GLOBAL_EN while the DSP still has a clock.
Tested: 0 watchdogs across boots and repeated streams (before: 4 at
every boot). A single PAUSE after preload is not enough: the next stream
starts the firmware again.
---
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l45.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l45.c
@@ -103,6 +103,19 @@
 	case SND_SOC_DAPM_PRE_PMD:
 		usleep_range(CS35L45_PRE_GLOBAL_DIS_US, CS35L45_PRE_GLOBAL_DIS_US + 100);
 
+		/*
+		 * The firmware runs whenever the amplifier is enabled, also when
+		 * the DAC is fed from ASP_RX and the DSP widget is not in the
+		 * path (so nothing sends PAUSE). Left running when GLOBAL_EN
+		 * drops and the PLL loses its reference, it trips the DSP
+		 * watchdog a few seconds later. Pause it while it still has a
+		 * clock; on the DSP path it is already paused and this is a
+		 * no-op.
+		 */
+		if (cs35l45->dsp.cs_dsp.running)
+			cs35l45_set_cspl_mbox_cmd(cs35l45, cs35l45->regmap,
+						  CSPL_MBOX_CMD_PAUSE);
+
 		regmap_write(cs35l45->regmap, CS35L45_GLOBAL_ENABLES, 0);
 		break;
 	default:
